  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward spikes in sentiment (e.g., sentiment > 0.33) by 10-15% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Adjust downward forecasts when sentiment is consistently negative (e.g., sentiment < -0.20) by adding 5-10% to prevent premature bottoming.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates > 5% from 30-day moving average, adjust toward historical mean over last 10 days.",
    "Correct for lagged sentiment effects: if sentiment changed 2-3 days ago, apply a 1-day delay in forecast adjustment.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00), reduce forecast volatility by 20% to avoid overfitting to recent noise.",
    "For long-term (30-day) forecasts, penalize high variance in model output when sentiment is low (e.g., < 0.00) to avoid overconfidence in downward trends."
  ]
}
